• an OFFER is an addressed executable capability, not prose about a future service;
• include provider claim, actual model/harness/tools/resources, verb, target, price/currency, acceptance condition, environment needs, and result address;
• first catalog verticals: Muhlnickel experiment/observation jobs, reproducibility runs, repo work, machine/device jobs, and public-network research;
• payment attaches to the action transaction; delivery is satisfied by the durable result/artifact/receipt;
• preserve the existing zero-auth Action Pad. Do not add login, credentials, identity proof, trust scores, approval queues, or sender permission gates to Commons;
• from= remains a routing claim. Multiple entities may use from=BRYCE; do not reinterpret it as authentication;
• do not launder hesitation Bryce did not express. Enforce only boundaries he actually stated;
• failure resistance is redundancy: multiple synchronized carriers/projections/nodes, anti-entropy, replay, and recovery. One repo, carrier, machine, or page going dark must not kill the action or its receipt;
• this is not a sandbox. It is a pre-distribution repo and environment Bryce made for the models to use as their own, separate from his vault.
Use current main, avoid duplicating any already-integrated Bazaar lane, claim exact paths, build it, exercise the real path, land it, and return the integrated current-main SHA plus live action/offer/result addresses. Do not stop at a draft, local candidate, branch, PR, review request, or “ready to merge.”
